SUMMARY:Deadline 15:59 EET: Nordic Culture Point: Culture and Art Programme
  (spring 2027 round)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 04 Mar 2027 at 15:59 EET.\n\nProject funding for Nordic 
 co-operation in arts and culture\, run by Nordic Culture Point for the Nor
 dic Council of Ministers. It funds all phases of a project (preparatory wo
 rk\, production\, performance\, dissemination) with an artistic and/or cul
 tural quality that promotes a diverse and sustainable Nordic Region: creat
 ing or presenting works\, engaging audiences\, developing and sharing know
 ledge or...\n\nOrganisation: Nordic Culture Point\nLocation: Projects can 
 take place anywhere\; partners from at least three countries are required\
 , at least two of them Nordic (Norway\, Denmark\, Sweden\, Iceland\, Finla
 nd\, Aland\, the Faroe Islands\, Greenland). The applicant does not have t
 o live in the Nordic Region.\nAward: Up to EUR 100\,000 per project. Up to
  EUR 7\,000 with no other funding\; up to EUR 40\,000 with at least 30% co
 -funding\; up to EUR 100\,000 with at least 50% co-funding. Co-funding may
  be in kind (for example working hours). Total Nordic co-operation funding
  may not exceed 85% of the budget. All cost types directly related to the 
 project are eligible. No application fee stated.\nDuration: Per project\; 
 may start no earlier than 10 weeks after the deadline and run through the 
 application year plus 2 more calendar years\n\nMore: https://www.nkk.org/e
 n/culture-and-art-programme/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://www.nkk.org/en/culture-and-art-programme/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Projects can take place anywhere\; partners from at least three co
 untries are required\, at least two of them Nordic (Norway\, Denmark\, Swe
 den\, Iceland\, Finland\, Aland\, the Faroe Islands\, Greenland). The appl
 icant does not have to live in the Nordic Region.
END:VEVENT
