SUMMARY:Deadline: DNA 2027\, Grenoble: open call for digital artworks (EUR 
 1\,000 fee plus travel\, accommodation and meals)
DESCRIPTION:DNA is the digital arts festival run by ARCAN in Grenoble under
  the motto 'arts numériques indisciplinés' (undisciplined digital arts).
  The 2027 edition is a three-day exhibition of installations and performan
 ces shown throughout\, plus one evening of performances. Any aesthetic is 
 welcome as long as the work has a digital element\; analogue electronics c
 ount.\n\nOrganisation: ARCAN\nLocation: Grenoble\, France. No nationality 
 or residency limit stated\; artists must be on site for the three festival
  days.\nAward: EUR 1\,000 total fee per exhibited work\, plus lunch and di
 nner from 20 to 23 May\, travel expenses and accommodation if needed. Cond
 itions for the performance evening are agreed case by case. No application
  fee mentioned.\nDuration: Festival 21 to 23 May 2027\; setup one or two d
 ays before\, takedown on 23 May or the day after.\n\nMore: https://arcan.i
 o/evenements/dna2027-appel/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://arcan.io/evenements/dna2027-appel/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Grenoble\, France. No nationality or residency limit stated\; arti
 sts must be on site for the three festival days.
END:VEVENT
